%% Azure Policy for Contoso landing zone - assignment, evaluation timing and the remediation task, including the branch where remediation fails
%% Source: Microsoft Learn "Remediate non-compliant resources" for managed identity, roleDefinitionIds and remediation task parameters, and "Get policy compliance data" for evaluation triggers and timings, both read 2026-09-03; the built-in GUIDs are the set listed in codex/blueprint-azure-files-secure-storage-account.md and codex/blueprint-azure-file-sync-private-path.md
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant PLT as Platform team - eng-netops
  participant POL as Azure Policy service
  participant MI as Assignment managed identity
  participant ARM as Azure Resource Manager
  participant RES as Contoso storage accounts and Storage Sync Services
  participant KIT as Assessment kit oracle

  Note over PLT,RES: The initiative assigned at Contoso landing-zone management group.<br/>Deny or Audit - 34c877ad network access, 6edd7eda private link, c9d007d0 trusted services,<br/>404c3081 secure transfer, fe83a0eb minimum TLS, e5612cea SMB encryption in transit,<br/>044985bb key expiry, 92a89a79 cross-tenant replication.<br/>Audit ONLY with an exemption for File Sync and Backup accounts - b2982f36 public network<br/>access and 8c6a50c6 shared key. Denying either one breaks sync or breaks backup.<br/>DeployIfNotExists and Modify for File Sync - b35dddd9 private endpoints, 0e07b2e9 disable public access.
  PLT->>POL: create the assignment at the management group scope
  POL->>MI: create the system-assigned identity for the deploy and modify effects
  alt assignment made in the portal
    POL->>MI: grant the roleDefinitionIds carried by the built-in definitions automatically
  else assignment made from the Bicep pipeline or an SDK
    Note over PLT,MI: Nothing is granted for you. The roles in roleDefinitionIds<br/>must be assigned to the identity by hand or every remediation fails later.
    PLT->>MI: az role assignment create for each roleDefinitionIds entry at the scope
  end
  POL-->>PLT: assignment reaches the scope after about 5 minutes, then evaluation starts

  Note over POL,RES: Two different clocks. A NEW or updated resource is evaluated on the write and<br/>its result appears in about 15 minutes. EXISTING resources are re-evaluated on the<br/>standard cycle once every 24 hours, and being marked non-compliant changes nothing<br/>on its own - deployIfNotExists and modify only touch existing resources through a remediation task.
  POL->>RES: standard evaluation cycle
  RES-->>POL: three storage accounts non-compliant on 6edd7eda, one Storage Sync Service on b35dddd9
  PLT->>POL: az policy state trigger-scan for the resource group, to avoid waiting for the daily cycle
  PLT->>POL: az policy remediation create for the deployIfNotExists assignment
  Note over PLT,POL: Remediation task settings that matter at Contoso scale.<br/>ResourceCount defaults to 500 and caps at 50000.<br/>ParallelDeploymentCount is 1 to 30 and defaults to 10.<br/>FailureThreshold defaults to 100 percent, so a task never fails fast unless you lower it.
  POL->>MI: run the embedded template as the assignment identity
  MI->>ARM: deploy the private endpoint and the DNS zone group

  alt the identity holds every role in roleDefinitionIds
    ARM->>RES: private endpoint created and approved
    RES-->>POL: compliance state Compliant on the next evaluation
    PLT->>KIT: re-export and re-assess the estate
    KIT-->>PLT: no SEC-03, no SEC-05, no AFS-11, no AFS-14 - the policy did what the blueprint says
  else a role is missing, or the target sits outside the assignment scope
    ARM-->>MI: deployment fails with an authorization error
    MI-->>POL: remediation resource marked failed, the resource stays non-compliant
    Note over PLT,ARM: This is the common failure. The private DNS zone lives in rg-dns-privatezones,<br/>outside the assignment scope, so Private DNS Zone Contributor was never granted there.
    PLT->>MI: grant the missing role at the zone resource group
    PLT->>POL: create the remediation task again
  end
  Note over PLT,KIT: Governance closure. A policy that only audits is a report, not a control.<br/>Record which definitions are Deny, which are Audit, and which accounts carry an<br/>exemption with its expiry date - an exemption with no expiry is undeclared drift.
